// Preserve #197's grief/condolence exchange and post-council recruitment.
// @12-16 supply the earlier palace context. Joining no longer assumes that
// the dukes have decided to send the player north.
@0 = ~You remember me, <CHARNAME>? Skie Silvershield. They buried my father while the whole city argued about this crusade. Everyone says I should sit in his empty house and mourn. I won't.~
@1 = ~I am sorry for your loss, Skie. Duke Silvershield was a pillar of this city.~
@2 = ~The dukes' council is no place for mourning, Skie. Why are you here?~
@3 = ~Because you're here. You're going after Caelar—everyone says so. Take me with you. I can open a lock and walk without a sound, and anything is better than sitting alone in Daddy's empty house.~
@4 = ~Very well, Skie. Gather your gear—we march north soon.~
@5 = ~No. A war camp is no place for you. Stay in Baldur's Gate.~
@6 = ~You mean it? You won't regret this, <CHARNAME>.~
@7 = ~Fine. FINE. Everyone decides what's best for Skie... I'll be here. Should you change your mind.~
@8 = ~Changed your mind, <CHARNAME>? Good. Take me with you—the offer stands.~
@9 = ~All right, Skie. Come along.~
@10 = ~Not yet, Skie.~
@11 = ~Thank you. You're going after Caelar—everyone says so. Take me with you. I can open a lock and walk without a sound, and anything is better than sitting alone in Daddy's empty house.~
@12 = ~Why are you here, Skie?~
@13 = ~Because you're here. Take me with you. I can open a lock and walk without a sound, and anything is better than sitting alone in Daddy's empty house.~
@14 = ~Thank you. Take me with you. I can open a lock and walk without a sound, and anything is better than sitting alone in Daddy's empty house.~
@15 = ~Very well, Skie. Gather your gear.~
@16 = ~Not now, Skie. Wait here.~
@17 = ~I'm ready when you are.~
